WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:05.400
Nothing transforms a good movie villain into
a great one like a killer wardrobe, a badass

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.300
backstory, and a compelling argument.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.120
These villains all had a pretty good point,
even if we were too busy hating them to realize

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:12.620
it.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.999
We should say up front that we firmly believe
The Dark Knight's Joker to be a raving sociopath

00:00:17.999 --> 00:00:20.130
and an absolute menace to society.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:24.909
But, hear us out, it's sometimes hard to argue
with his philosophy that human beings are

00:00:24.909 --> 00:00:28.020
not meant to be confined within a structured
society.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.960
And yes, human beings find ways to remind
us of the delicate nature of social contracts

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:33.780
every day.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.700
"You see: this is how crazy Batman's made
Gotham.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.520
You want order in Gotham?

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.180
Batman must take off his mask and turn himself
in.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.320
Oh, and everyday he doesn't, people will die."

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:52.170
Joker's ferry vs. ferry experiment may have
failed to bring Gotham to its knees, but that

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:55.539
doesn't mean he wasn't right about a certain
Gothamite's nature.

00:00:55.539 --> 00:00:59.879
Yup, we're talking about D.A. Harvey Dent,
better known as "Two Face."

00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:04.470
Joker tortured the noble law man emotionally
and physically early in the film before breaking

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:07.860
Dent's psyche and turning him loose on a coin-flipping
killing spree.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:11.640
Bringing Gotham's Golden Boy down into the
trenches with the rest of the city's criminals

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.070
was Joker's masterpiece.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.680
It was only tarnished by Batman and Chief
Gordon spinning the biggest web of lies that

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.000
Gotham has ever seen… which sort of feels
like a loss for the supposed good guys.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:27.170
Count yourself lucky if you are not the leader
of the free world when the apocalypse begins.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:32.100
That's just where Carl Anheuser found himself
when the end began in the brainless disaster

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.360
flick 2012.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.520
"Just exactly how long are these things expecting
to hold us in place, Captain?"

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:40.460
"They're just meant to withstand the first
impact of the waves, Mr. Anheuser."

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:45.039
While Anheuser was an antagonistic presence
throughout the film, he didn't achieve full

00:01:45.039 --> 00:01:50.100
on villain status until he thwarted the heroic
efforts of Jackson Curtis to save his family

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:55.660
by unceremoniously slamming the door to salvation
in the Curtis family's collective faces.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:59.980
It's a brutal moment to be sure, but it's
important to remember that if Anheuser hadn't

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:03.979
shut the doors, the world-ending flood outside
might have found its way in.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:06.840
It would have killed all of the would-be survivors
aboard the Ark.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.360
And that would've meant the end of humanity.

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:13.660
So yeah, Anheuser could've been nicer about
everything, but seriously, he had to close

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:14.460
those doors.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:20.220
Sure, Daniel Craig plays an excellent Bond,
but the success of 2012's box office-smashing

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:26.830
Skyfall owes a lot to Javier Bardem's performance
as scorned secret agent turned vengeful cyber-terrorist

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:27.830
Raoul Silva.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:32.100
While there's no question that Silva falls
on the baddie side of the spectrum, he's also,

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.180
well, a human.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.620
A terrible, awful, no-good human, but a human
nonetheless.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:40.560
"I win.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.000
What do you say to that?"

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:46.280
"...A waste of good scotch."

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:50.620
He's talented, sure, and he's hyper-intelligent,
but he's also tortured.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:51.460
Sound familiar?

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:56.220
There are definite parallels between Silva,
a former MI6 agent who was abandoned to be

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.200
tortured by the Chinese, and Bond.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:02.320
In fact, it was Silva's sympathetic backstory
that attracted Bardem to the part.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.080
The actor told Fox News:

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.590
"Here there is a broken person.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:08.560
What I like the most is there is a clear motive.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.780
We understand he is very human and this is
powerful.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.650
I was attracted to the villain because I thought
he was a nice guy.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:16.000
I could see it in his eyes."

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:20.520
We're not sure we agree with Bardem, but we'll
admit Silva's about as sympathetic as Bond

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.840
villains get, and that's got to count for
something.

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:38.000
He was one of the biggest action heroes of
the day, but if Top Gun were real life, there's

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.000
no way that Tom Cruise's Pete "Maverick" Mitchell
would be a popular guy.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:47.190
The antagonist of the '80s classic, Val Kilmer's
Tom "Iceman" Kazansky, on the other hand,

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:48.220
very well might be.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:53.320
As top dog at the Naval Air Station Miramar
Top Gun school, he's spent years training

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:57.670
to be the best young pilot around, so of course
he's going to have a problem when this upstart

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:01.400
Maverick turns up and displays a blatant disregard
for everyone's safety.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:03.100
"You guys really are cowboys."

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.300
"What's your problem, Kazansky?"

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.600
"You're everyone's problem, that's because
everytime you go up in the air, you're unsafe."

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:15.940
At one stage, reports emerged suggesting that
Cruise and Kilmer's on-set relationship mirrored

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:19.969
that of their characters, but if there was
ever any truth to this then it's clearly all

00:04:19.969 --> 00:04:23.600
water under the bridge, as the pair are reuniting
for Top Gun 2.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:27.720
Kilmer was sidelined with throat cancer for
a while, but he has revealed that he's fit

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:31.180
and well enough to reprise the role of Iceman
in the upcoming sequel.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.460
"I don't like you because you're dangerous."

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:33.960
"That's right, Iceman.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:39.000
I am dangerous."

